{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Re-probe 03:38 UTC (20:38 PDT): no recovery merge since 03:20:50; HEAD unchanged at `0ffc807745`, now 11 ahead / 20 behind `origin/tickets` (`68d42e33f2`). Observation: the two earlier merges coincided with MCP-side writes (the push path runs its recovery cycles after a write), and since all lanes moved to the local CLI nothing has written through MCP, so nothing triggers the server's push. The `run_ensures` sweep is not producing sync lines either. Conclusion: the clone will not converge on its own while MCP is idle; it needs either a normal MCP write (this comment is one, posted through the MCP server deliberately to exercise the push recovery against a now-quieter origin) or the operator push on the container. If this comment appears on `origin/tickets` within a few minutes, the recovery path works and the incident is a liveness gap (no idle-time sync), to be fixed under AC6."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792381261223287022,"uuid":"be38f5f6-a251-40fe-8972-e5484fe7b0f9"}